cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Epistemic Crucible benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Success Is Not Identification: Crossed World Interventions for Attributing Agent Policies"
abstract: >-
  A crossed-intervention behavioral assay that measures whether an interactive
  policy's terminal choices track operative detector evidence or a correlated visible
  cue. It makes no claim about internal representations or causal knowledge and
  reports an unaggregated vector of paired attribution metrics.
type: software
authors:
